The base side length of the first pyramid is $\blueD{\sqrt{\dfrac{3V}{h}}}$.

Let's take $\sqrt{\dfrac{3V}{\goldD h}}$ and replace $\goldD h$ with $\goldD{4h}$:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{\dfrac{3V}{(\goldD{4h})}}&=\sqrt{\dfrac14\cdot\dfrac{3V}{h}}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{\dfrac14}\cdot\sqrt{\dfrac{3V}{h}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac12\left(\blueD{\sqrt{\dfrac{3V}{h}}}\right)
\end{align}$

We started with an expression where $h$ is increased by a factor of $4$ and ended with the overall expression decreased by a factor of $2$.
